CON-19: divide the swale and pavement surface flux by the vegetation void fraction

The surface layer's water fills only the fraction 1 - VegFrac of the space
above the surface. swaleFluxRates() and pavementFluxRates() book the stored
surface volume with that void fraction but advanced the surface depth with
the net inflow rate alone, so with VegFrac > 0 only part of the net inflow
showed up as storage and the rest was lost from the water balance (or
created when the surface drained). Divide the surface depth rate by the
void fraction, as biocellFluxRates(), trenchFluxRates() and the reference
manual's surface layer equation already do. Nothing changes when VegFrac = 0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-19_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c b/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
index dbd83e4..cae91ae 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lidproc.c
@@ -1039,7 +1039,8 @@ void pavementFluxRates(double x[], double f[])
     SurfaceOutflow = getSurfaceOutflowRate(surfaceDepth);
 
     //... compute overall layer flux rates
-    f[SURF] = SurfaceInflow - SurfaceEvap - SurfaceInfil - SurfaceOutflow;
+    f[SURF] = (SurfaceInflow - SurfaceEvap - SurfaceInfil - SurfaceOutflow) /
+              theLidProc->surface.voidFrac;
     f[PAVE] = (SurfaceInfil - PaveEvap - PavePerc) / paveVoidFrac;
     if ( theLidProc->soil.thickness > 0.0)
     {
@@ -1161,7 +1162,7 @@ void swaleFluxRates(double x[], double f[])
     SurfaceEvap /= lidArea;
     StorageExfil /= lidArea;
     SurfaceOutflow /= lidArea;
-    f[SURF] = dVdT / surfArea;
+    f[SURF] = dVdT / (surfArea * theLidProc->surface.voidFrac);
     f[SOIL] = 0.0;
     f[STOR] = 0.0;
 
